The valley is covered with mist, and dusk has already fallen. You and your friends—Doyle, Conan, and Irene—are making their way through the coastal shrubbery, closer and closer to the edge of the island. Black, crooked branches often emerge from the fog, swaying as if alive. It's cool outside, and a chilly wind is blowing. Sometimes you can hear grinding sounds, typical of the floating of ice when the edges of ice blocks clash.

Finally, you pass through the shrubbery and come to the edge of the island. Usually, it resembles the edge of a chasm, but today everything is different. Today, an unknown and mysterious land is floating past the edge of your home. This is the famous Wild Island where Cyrus Paganel was on an expedition. You've heard about it many times, and now you see the island with your own eyes.

"Quickly!" screams Conan. "Or we won't make it!"

Your friends run towards the edge and jump over one by one. Even Doyle is already on the other side, waving to you.

"Henry! Come to us."

You run towards them. There is the edge of the island, there is the fearsome chasm. Wild Island is slowly drifting ahead, resembling a black river.

