[MUSIC: another_world_day_5.ogg]

"Snoopy, stop, Snoopy!"
Without thinking about the danger, you rush after your loyal friend. With a single jump, you cross the roaring precipice. Once again, Snoopy's silhouette flickers among the trees and disappears behind them.
A few adults, who saw your desperate act, run towards you, screaming something. You continue to rush after Snoopy, moving deeper into the unfamiliar forest, guided by distant barking. Although you run as fast as possible, the barking becomes more and more distant. Eventually, you're out of breath, feeling pain in your chest; you have no more strength to keep running.
The Wild Island forest surrounds you, and you instantly realize that you've gone too far. It's necessary to return for help, but it's not so easy to find the way back. You could follow your trail, but there is a dense carpet of musty foliage on the ground, making it impossible to see any footprints. You try to listen for the roar of clashing edges of two islands, but it is lost in the noise of disturbed inhabitants of the forest. It seems you're completely lost.

